<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Montgomery</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1267">1267</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Montgomery was agreed on 29 September 1267 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-of-england">Henry III of England</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llywelyn-ap-gruffudd">Llywelyn ap Gruffudd</a>, brokered by the papal legate Ottobuono. Henry recognised Llywelyn as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-wales">Prince of Wales</a>, with overlordship over the other Welsh lords, in return for homage and a large payment. It marked the height of the native Welsh principality, but disputes over the payments and homage led to Edward I's invasion of 1277.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-montgomery.jpg" alt="Treaty of Montgomery" width="320" height="453" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: A455bcd9 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wales_after_the_Treaty_of_Montgomery_1267_Colorblind.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
